From 68cf8fc7a9f6ad6e3b74c29445996bc447be4864 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:08:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 65/71] sniff: uTP only at the start of a connection, and the
 DHT of BitTorrent

uTP is taken only from a SYN of version 1 with a timestamp difference of 0 and extensions that end
exactly at the end of the packet, as Xray takes it. A data packet cannot be told from one packet: a
plain WireGuard handshake initiation reads as one without extensions and began every WireGuard
tunnel taken for BitTorrent, and about one random packet in 6,400 passed the check (D-49).

DHT is a new packet sniffer, before uTP: the whole packet one bencoded dictionary of KRPC (BEP 5)
with a transaction id and a query (with its method and arguments), a response or an error. A
client sends DHT, uTP and the UDP tracker over one socket, and its first packet is a DHT query
(qBittorrent, Transmission, aria2, rTorrent on the stand of 2026-10-12), which decides the
protocol of the whole socket: before, every client's socket was sniffed as nothing.

Pdk-Feature: sniff-bittorrent
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 06
